      "purpose": "ILE RPG program (RPROPNFLD) that repairs invalid OPEN fields caused by DBCS character truncation in a database file. It dynamically opens a named database file using low-level MIH/DM routines (QDMCOPEN/QDMCLOSE via SEPT), reads each record, checks for truncated DBCS shift-out/shift-in sequences in a specified field position and length, repairs the data in-place, and updates the record. Part of the i5/OS Programmer's Toolkit open-source project.",
